# Amendment #75 — A1 substrate timestamp-format normalization

2026-04-28. Per the locked plan-doc
`docs/rebuild/plans/a1-substrate-timestamp-format-normalization.md`
and locked research artefact
`docs/rebuild/plans/research/a1-substrate-timestamp-format-normalization-research.md`.
Composes on the four-amendment structural-enforcement programme
(A1 #51 substrate; A2 #70 objective-binding gate; A3 #71 TDD-guard;
A4 #72 Bash/Agent guards) plus #52, #73, #74. No programme
amendment; this is a substrate-layer defect-class fix per ODD
§5.1.1 elimination.

This amendment closes the failure class flagged in FIDRAFT
line 155 (captured 2026-04-28 by amendment #74's build agent).
A1's substrate shipped two lexicographically-incomparable
timestamp formats: the sentinels emitted second-resolution
`%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ`; the manifest emitted microsecond
`%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S.%f+00:00`. On same-second writes lex-compare
flipped because `.` (0x2E) sorts before `Z` (0x5A) — A3's
`manifest_row.created_at > sentinel.created_at` predicate
silently produced `False` for legitimate new-AC rows. Empirical
pre-fix: 1000/1000 collisions in tight-loop test (FIDRAFT 155).

Resolution per ODD §5.1.1 elimination: migrate ALL THREE A1
timestamp emitters to format γ — microsecond-resolution,
`Z`-suffixed, fixed-width 27 chars
(`%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S.%fZ`). The fixed width matters because
`strftime`'s `%f` always emits 6 digits, removing the
`isoformat()` zero-microsecond stripping edge case.

